# Onboarding extraction — rent roll vs lease

## Source of truth

| Document | Creates Properties / Units / Residents | Lease Information Found |
|---|---|---|
| **Rent roll** (or resident roster) | **Yes** — portfolio SoT | No (ignore invented `leases[]`) |
| **Lease agreement** | **Never** | Yes — enrich matched rent-roll residents |
| **Unknown** type | **Never** — flag for review | No |

## Matching

Before applying lease fields, match the lease tenant to a rent-roll resident using property + unit + name (and phone/email when present). Formatting differences (`Unit 2A` / `2A`, `John Smith` / `John A. Smith`) are OK when unit/property evidence agrees.

- **Match** → merge lease dates / missing rent onto the same resident (no duplicate).
- **No match** → keep lease in Lease Information (needs review); **do not** mint a resident or unit.
- **Rent conflict** → keep rent-roll amount; surface `rent_amount_conflict` for review.

## Processing order

Classify each file → extract rent rolls → build portfolio → extract leases → match/enrich → flag conflicts & unmatched.

## Where it lives

`src/lib/onboardingDocumentUpload.ts` — `classifyOnboardingDocumentExtractRole`, `mergeExtractedDocuments`, `fillExtractedResidentsFromLeases`

## Do not

- Create a resident, unit, or property from a lease alone
- Treat the whole upload batch as one document type
- Silently overwrite rent-roll rent with a conflicting lease amount
